          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p The original article:
          %ul
            %li#Girard1987
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Yves+Girard"}> Jean-Yves Girard
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Linear logic
              %strong 50
              1 (1987) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0304-3975(87)90045-4"}> doi:10.1016/0304-3975(87)90045-4
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://iml.univ-mrs.fr/~girard/linear.pdf"} pdf
          %p Review:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anne+Sjerp+Troelstra"}> Anne Sjerp Troelstra
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Lectures on Linear Logic
                %strong 29
                (1992) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://web.stanford.edu/group/cslipublications/cslipublications/site/0937073776.shtml"}> ISBN:0937073776
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frank+Pfenning"}> Frank Pfenning
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Linear Logic
                %strong 29
                (1998) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://www.cs.cmu.edu/~fp/courses/98-linear/handouts/notes.pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.cs.cmu.edu/~fp/courses/98-linear/handouts.html"} webpage
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Pfenning-LinearLogic98.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Yves+Girard"}> Jean-Yves Girard
                ,
                %em Linear logic, its syntax and semantics
                (2006) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://www.cs.brandeis.edu/~cs112/2006-cs112/docs/girard-intro.pdf"}> pdf
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#Girard11
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Yves+Girard"}> Jean-Yves Girard
                , part III of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lectures+on+Logic"} Lectures on Logic
            %li{:id => "MihályiNovitzká13"}
              %p
                Daniel Mihályi, Valerie Novitzká,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em What about Linear Logic in Computer Science?
                %strong 10
                4 (2013) 147-160 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://acta.uni-obuda.hu/Mihalyi_Novitzka_42.pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/MihalyiNovitzka-LinearLogic.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            and making explicit the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
            of linear logic in the category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FinDimVect"} FinDimVect
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite-dimensional+vector+spaces"} finite-dimensional vector spaces
          %ul
            %li#Pratt93
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vaughan+Pratt"}> Vaughan Pratt
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The second calculus of binary relations
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 711
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/3-540-57182-5_9"} doi:10.1007/3-540-57182-5_9
              %blockquote
                %p
                  “Linear logic is seen in its best light as the realization of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Curry-Howard+isomorphism"} Curry-Howard isomorphism
                  for
                  = succeed "\u201D" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+algebra"} linear algebra
            %li#ValironZdancewic14
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Beno%C3%AEt+Valiron"}> Benoît Valiron
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Steve+Zdancewic"} Steve Zdancewic
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Finite Vector Spaces as Model of Simply-Typed Lambda-Calculi
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Proc. of ICTAC’14
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 8687
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1406.1310"} arXiv:1406.1310
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-319-10882-7_26"} doi:10.1007/978-3-319-10882-7_26
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.cs.bham.ac.uk/~drg/bll/steve.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Zdancewic-LinearLogicAlgebra.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li#Murfet14
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Murfet"}> Daniel Murfet
                ,
                %em Logic and linear algebra: an introduction
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1407.2650"}> arXiv:1407.2650
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            following a remark in section 2.4.2 of
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#HylandSchalk03"} Hyland &amp; Schalk (2003)
          %ul
            %li#HylandSchalk03
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Hyland"}> Martin Hyland
                , Andrea Schalk,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Glueing and orthogonality for models of linear logic
                %strong 294
                1–2 (2003) 183-231 [
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/S0304-3975(01)00241-9"}> doi:10.1016/S0304-3975(01)00241-9
                ]
            %li
              %p
                Wikipedia:
                %em
                  %a{:href => "https://secure.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/wiki/Linear_logic"} Linear Logic
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
            of linear logic in general
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/star-autonomous+categories"} star-autonomous categories
            originally appeared in
          %ul
            %li#Seely
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/R.+A.+G.+Seely"}> R. A. G. Seely
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Linear logic,
                    = succeed "-autonomous" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mo *
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ast
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Categories in Computer Science and Logic
                %strong 92
                (1989) &amp;lbrack;
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/SeelyLinearLogic.pdf", :title => "pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.mcgill.ca/rags/nets/llsac.ps.gz"} ps.gz
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://bookstore.ams.org/conm-92"} ISBN:978-0-8218-5100-5
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Barr"}> Michael Barr
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo *
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ast
                    \-Autonomous categories and linear logic
                %strong 1
                2 (1991) 159–178 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/S0960129500001274"}> doi:10.1017/S0960129500001274
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.math.mcgill.ca/barr/papers/scatll.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Barr-AutomomousCatAndLinLogic.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            and for the special case of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantales"} quantales
            in
          %ul
            %li#Yetter90
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Yetter"}> David Yetter
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Quantales and (noncommutative) linear logic
          %p
            and further in view of the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chu+construction"} Chu construction
          %ul
            %li#Pratt93
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vaughan+Pratt"}> Vaughan Pratt
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The second calculus of binary relations
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 711
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/3-540-57182-5_9"} doi:10.1007/3-540-57182-5_9
            %li#Pratt99
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vaughan+Pratt"}> Vaughan Pratt
                ,
                %em Chu Spaces
                (1999) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://boole.stanford.edu/pub/coimbra.pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Pratt-ChuSpaces.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            The more general case of of multiplicative intuitionistic linear logic interpreted more generally in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+categories"} symmetric monoidal categories
            was systematically developed in
          %ul
            %li#Szabo78
              M.E. Szabo,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Algebra of Proofs
          %blockquote
            %p (that was before Girard introduced the “linear” terminology).
          %p More recent articles exploring this:
          %ul
            %li#dePaiva89
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Valeria+de+Paiva"}> Valeria de Paiva
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Dialectica Categories
                %em Contemporary Mathematics
                92, 1989. (
                %a{:href => "http://www.cs.bham.ac.uk/~vdp/publications/dial87.pdf"}> web
                )
            %li#Blute91
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+Blute"}> Richard Blute
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Linear logic, coherence, and dinaturality
              %p Volume 115 Issue 1, July 5, 1993 Pages 3–41
            %li#BentonBiermanPaivaHyland92
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nick+Benton"}> Nick Benton
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gavin+Bierman"} Gavin Bierman
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Valeria+de+Paiva"} Valeria de Paiva
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Hyland"} Martin Hyland
                = succeed "." do
                  %em Term assignments for intuitionistic linear logic
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://citeseerx.ist.psu.edu/viewdoc/summary?doi=10.1.1.31.8666"} citeseer
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.cs.bham.ac.uk/~vdp/publications/tr262.ps"} ps
            %li#HylandPaiva93
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Hyland"}> Martin Hyland
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Valeria+de+Paiva"} Valeria de Paiva
                %em Full Intuitionistic Linear Logic
                (extended abstract). Annals of Pure and Applied Logic, 64(3), pp. 273–291, 1993. (
                %a{:href => "http://www.cs.bham.ac.uk/~vdp/publications/fill.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li#Bierman95
              %p
                G. Bierman,
                %em On Intuitionistic Linear Logic
                PhD thesis, Computing Laboratory, University of Cambridge, 1995 (
                %a{:href => "https://citeseerx.ist.psu.edu/viewdoc/download?doi=10.1.1.114.588&rep=rep1&type=pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li#Barber97
              %p
                Andrew Graham Barber,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Linear Type Theories, Semantics and Action Calculi
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.lfcs.inf.ed.ac.uk/reports/97/ECS-LFCS-97-371/&#8206;"} web
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.lfcs.inf.ed.ac.uk/reports/97/ECS-LFCS-97-371/ECS-LFCS-97-371.pdf"} pdf
          %p This is reviewed/further discussed in
          %ul
            %li#Schalk04
              %p
                Andrea Schalk,
                %em What is a categorical model for linear logic?
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.cs.man.ac.uk/~schalk/notes/llmodel.pdf"}> pdf
